gaps.proposal:
One action, inspect {spark, probe}, in a new part 20-inspect.mjs. Probes are fixed shell snippets sent through run(), like LINKS_SCRIPT; the caller sends only a probe's name. They do not go in worker.py, which is hashed into every workflow version and sent as one 45 KB argument.
First probes:
- network: every interface classed from /sys as wired, Wi-Fi, 200G cable or Tailscale, with carrier, speed, address, bound driver and default route;
- versions: kernel, DGX OS, GPU driver, Docker, container toolkit, Tailscale, pending upgrades from apt-get -s, the package lists' age, reboot waiting, firmware waiting;
- disk: total, used, free, and models, images, caches and partial downloads, each marked as Spark Console's leftover or yours;
- gpu: memory by container, reusing gpuUsersScript (05-library.mjs:142-147);
- services: failed units and clock sync; on Spark 2 also the console unit, watchdog, linger, build and last backup;
- tailscale: each Spark's key expiry, from the status Spark 2 already fetches;
- health: today's diagnostics, so spark_diagnostics goes and the count stays 36.
Each result has observedAt and couldNotRead.
