gaps.whyItMatters:
Verified examples:
- catalog.json is stamped 2026-11-04 by a fixed string (tools/build-catalog.py:266);
- default engine images are bare digests with no version or date (service/config.json:27-30);
- a recipe source that moves returns an empty list, read as "0 found";
- Spark 1 is still listed and retried (service/config.json:7);
- contract 9.17 (fleet care, expiries) is unbuilt.
The owner has no single question to ask. Worth it for one owner: one read replaces remembering to look in ten places, with no notifications.

gaps.proposal:
New part 20-fresh.mjs: one daily look, run as one operation with one event. The setups looks run inside it, and its summary says what is new. It serves whats_outdated: at most ten items, each with what, since when, how it knows, the next step and who decides.
It checks:
- memory lines whose check now differs;
- held entries older than 7 days;
- saved workflows that fail a dry check;
- a setups source that returns nothing where it used to;
- a catalog older than 45 days, and models NVIDIA has a Spark recipe for that Recipes lacks;
- a newer release of an engine in use (weekly, releases only);
- per Spark: pending upgrades, a waiting reboot, and Sparks 3 and 4 on different kernels or drivers;
- a Tailscale key inside 14 days;
- a running build that differs from the source on Spark 2;
- a Spark unseen for 30 days.
